   ["THE CORPUS CHECK READ A KEY THE TRACE NEVER WRITES, AND CALLED THE RESULT AN ABSENCE. The delivered D3 looked for the posterior under [:decision :softmax-weights] and reported 'persisted :softmax-weights: zero', then fell back to reconstructing an ordering from the retained :selection-score for all 95 records it could use. That key is dissoc'd by construction -- trace.clj:167-177 drops it because its keys are action MAPS, and re-keys Q(pi) by the rank/N of the record's outer :ranked-actions when policy trace details are on. So the posterior IS persisted: 74 records carry it (wm-trace-2026-09-01.edn), 74 of 74 resolve back to actions through :ranked-actions (trace.clj:150-155, the same join run9_s4_arms.clj:47-60 makes), and the delivered check discarded all of them. Fixed: posterior-result now reads the persisted posterior first and reconstructs only where none was written. The population rises 95 -> 98 (the 3 F_pi-applied records no longer have to be dropped), and where both representations exist they order the head identically in 71 of 71."
    "THE LEAN FINDING WAS AN ARTEFACT OF THE HARNESS'S OWN EXTRACTION. The delivered check recorded :positive-source-drift because Holes.softmax mismatched its pinned hash. The span it hashes runs from the declaration line to the START of the next declaration -- and a docstring opener is not a boundary in that rule, so every span carries the NEXT declaration's prose. What changed is exactly that prose: mathlib4 6dabfb686f (U29, 're-resolve the glossary owner pointers') rewrote bayesianModelReduction's docstring owner from sec-glossary.tex:54 to :58. The def softmax body is byte-identical across that commit. Fixed: a drift localiser that asks git which commit last touched the span's lines, checks that commit's PARENT span against the pin (it matches) and its body against HEAD's body (unchanged), and reports :locus :neighbour-docstring-inside-the-span. The finding is now :pinned-span-moved-outside-the-declaration-body, and a fifth plant edits the def line of an in-memory copy to prove the localiser still calls a real body change a body change."
    "A PINNED LINE RANGE INSIDE THE MEASUREMENT, the same defect slice 9's review found twice. The F_pi site census filtered occurrences to the literal range 208-213, so a line shift in policy.clj would have been read as 'no application site' -- a :fail reporting an absence. Fixed: the application site is now derived from the shape of two adjacent lines (the flag, and a subtraction of the F term on the next line), and the registry's OWN claim about where the score expression lives (aif-equations.edn:177, ':208-213') is checked against the derived line instead of being used as the search. Derived site: policy.clj:211, inside the declared range."
    "TWO CARRIER POINTERS OVERRAN THEIR SUBJECT. sim/R6-carriers.edn declared :posterior at aif-equations.edn:173-181, but R6's :policy-posterior row ends at :178 and :179-181 is R16's :action row -- a different node. And :candidate-construction pointed at war_machine.clj:6278-6304, which is candidate ENRICHMENT; construction is the compose-proposers call at :6267-6277. Both corrected."
