   :the-node-itself-is-arithmetically-right
   "SAID PLAINLY, BECAUSE THE HOLE ABOVE COULD BE MISREAD AS ONE: nothing here says the belief update computes the wrong thing. The composite the registry's :lean-note describes is what the machine runs, and it agrees with an independent reference everywhere this slice can compare it -- the multichannel driver at deviation exactly 0.0 on exact dyadic fixtures, the single-channel driver exactly, all four :unknown reasons reproduced with no :driver on any of them, the tempered filter within 5.55e-17 against a tolerance of 1e-15 (and exactly 0.0 in the kappa(0) case where Bayes must leave the prior fixed), and the per-entity attribution's mean equal to the event weight at deviation 0.0. In production the two arithmetic identities hold on EVERY entry the corpus has: anneal-factor = max(0, 1 - step/3) at max deviation 0.0 over 2634, and event-weight = min(1,|driver|) x anneal x 0.1 at max deviation 0.0 over 2622. Eight planted wrong nodes -- an arithmetic-mean driver, a signless driver, a count-divisor driver, a zero-instead-of-unknown driver, an invented :refused third status, kappa = w, a filter that substitutes a non-identity prediction step, and an anneal of 1 - step/2 -- are ALL caught."

   :stated-limits
   [{:limit :the-clamp-discards-the-magnitude-on-85-percent-of-the-recorded-history
     :statement "THE SHARPEST THING THE CORPUS SAYS ABOUT THIS NODE. base-weight is (min 1.0 aggregated-magnitude) (scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:6160), so on any micro-step whose |driver| reaches 1 the size of the surprise is discarded and only its sign reaches belief. MEASURED over every micro-step entry ever recorded: 2232 of 2622 saturate -- 85.1%. The split is total and lands on the multichannel flag. Of the 2232 entries in the 43 files from wm-trace-2026-05-19.edn to wm-trace-2026-07-06.edn, ONE HUNDRED PERCENT saturate, with |driver| between 40.17 and 74.02; of the 390 entries in the 13 files from wm-trace-2026-07-09.edn to wm-trace-2026-09-04.edn, NONE do, with |driver| between 4.08e-4 and 0.226. THE REASON IS THE REGISTRY'S OWN LEAN PROPERTY, and this is the corpus measuring what Lean proved possible: the single-channel driver IS a channel's weighted error, error x precision with precision = 1/max(v,0.01) and so up to 100x, while the multichannel driver divides by the sum of the precisions, which cancels that scale (precisionScalesSingleChannel and precisionDividesOutInMultichannel, both named at aif-equations.edn:117). Arming the flag on 2026-07-08 therefore changed the driver's units by about three orders of magnitude, and with them changed the clamp from always-binding to never-binding. WHAT IT BEARS ON: p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:198 states R3's invariant as moving belief toward the observation 'only as far as the learning rate and the trust placed in that channel allow'. For 43 of the corpus's 57 files, neither the trust nor the size of the error reached belief -- only the sign did, and the event weight was exactly the anneal factor times 0.1 on every one of those steps."
     :where "the :magnitude-saturation key of holes/labs/wm-contract/runs/V7-R3-node-sim/00-r3.edn, including its per-file table"
     :not-repaired "Changing the clamp, or recording that the flag flip rescaled the driver, is a change to the machine or a ruling. Neither is a slice of :V7. Recorded."}

    {:limit :the-typed-unknown-driver-has-never-fired-and-its-absence-encoding-is-era-dependent
     :statement "AC2's :unknown driver -- the ruling's shape, where a tick with no contributing channel applies NO belief event rather than a fabricated zero -- has ZERO production inhabitants. The tick writes :aggregated-driver-unknown with the reason whenever the aggregator reports :unknown (scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:6209-6211); that key occurs on 0 of 2634 micro-step entries. SEPARATELY, the code's stated rule for reading the absence does not hold over the whole corpus. The comment at scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:6198-6200 says 'No key means the aggregator reported :unknown'. Twelve entries carry no :aggregated-signed-error, and none of them is an :unknown record: all twelve are in wm-trace-2026-05-19.edn (record indices 4-7, steps 0-2), none carries :aggregated-driver-unknown, and each carries :events-applied 47 with an :event-weight of exactly anneal x 0.1 -- so events WERE applied and the driver saturated, which is the opposite of what the rule would have a reader conclude. They predate the key. A reader applying HEAD's rule to the archive misreads twelve entries as refusals."
     :where "the :absent-driver-key key of the receipt, which lists all twelve"}

    {:limit :alpha-has-no-named-inhabitant
     :statement "aif-equations.edn:67 declares :alpha as an exogenous symbol, 'belief-update step size', :class :stack-defined -- the War Machine supplies the content. What supplies it is the bare literal 0.1 inside an arithmetic expression (scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj:6161), with no var, no name and no docstring; grep over src/futon2/aif/belief.clj and scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj for learning-rate, r3-alpha and belief-alpha returns nothing. p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:198 asks for belief updates that are 'tunable (one learning rate; a separate trust setting per evidence channel)'. The per-channel trust is a named registry (R7); the one learning rate is a magic number. Stated, not repaired: naming it is a change to the machine."}

    {:limit :the-fixture-leg-is-thin-and-the-production-leg-is-what-carries-the-slice
     :statement "The fixture side is deliberately small: 2 driver comparisons, 3 filter comparisons and 3 attribution entities, against slice 2's 224 comparisons and slice 3's 36. It is exact where it can be -- the driver fixtures are dyadic and compare at 0.0 -- but it is a handful of cases, and the eight plants are what establish that those cases discriminate. The weight of this slice is the replay: 2634 entries re-derived from their own recorded fields, which is a check of the shipped tick and not of a fixture."}

