   :the-document-staleness-reaches-eight-sites
   "docs/futon-aif-completeness.md reports R3a's coverage as four of fourteen at :86, :90, :106, :181, :194, :342, :360 and :391, against the eight the node ships. Slice 5 recorded the :86 under-report as part of R3's hole; what this slice adds is that the same count is repeated at seven further sites, including the R7 grade at :181 and :194, which inherits it -- R7 is 'satisfied for the 4 channels that have R3a likelihood' and there are eight. AND ONE SITE NAMES AS OUTSTANDING A THING THAT SHIPPED: :360's 'Load-bearing remaining work for the v1.0 contract' lists '(b) R3a likelihood model so the trace's :prediction-errors field becomes meaningful', where slice 3 measured :prediction-errors on 887 of 889 records and this slice measures 6537 persisted entries in them. Recorded as a finding, not repaired: document edits sit behind the TN 9a review gate."

   :stated-limits
   ["THE HARNESS HOLDS NO INDEPENDENT ARITHMETIC REFERENCE FOR eps, BY DESIGN, AND THAT IS ITS SHARPEST LIMIT. Slice 3 owns the eps arithmetic at R8 and re-deriving it here would have duplicated rather than added. The consequence is measured and recorded in the receipt rather than left implicit: the plant :sign-flipped-error is caught only because it desynchronises the scalar form from the envelope form, and a probe applying the same flip to BOTH forms at once fails nothing in this harness. It is recorded as :sign-flipped-in-both-forms, a :discrimination-limit with :would-be-caught false computed rather than asserted. This harness establishes that the two forms agree and that the typed statuses behave; it does not establish the sign convention."
    "THE CARRIERS FILE'S EIGHT-MEMBER LIST IS TRANSCRIBED FROM THE NODE'S OWN DEFINITION SITE. The pair receipt declares :channels-delivered 8 without naming them and the completeness document names four, so belief.clj:919-934 is the only place the eight are written down; the harness's channel check therefore compares the live var against a hand transcription of that var's own literal. What is genuinely independent in that check is the subset-of-fourteen relation (the fourteen come from observation.clj:18-31) and the six-member complement -- and the complement is corroborated outside the harness by the F8 readback, which names the same six."
    "The corpus half of the harness has no negative control. The nine plants substitute the node and are run against the fixture checks only; no plant perturbs the trace. What guards the corpus numbers instead is that this seat wrote and ran an independent probe before the bellback arrived and the two agree digit-for-digit on every published total."
