   :the-verdict-rests-on-what-the-corpus-was-produced-by
   {:the-measurement "6534 persisted per-channel precision values. 1032 agree with the shipped map at deviation exactly 0.0. 5502 do not, and the disagreement is not noise: 5494 of the 5494 mismatching states that carry both components have a :variance-component equal to the SUPERSEDED producer's form, and 5494 of 5494 have a stored precision equal to bounded(:variance-component + :need-component), the :summed salience mode. Both references were transcribed into the harness from futon2 9d8f2dee^, not read off the node (receipt :production-M4b)."
    :the-break-is-read-off-the-corpus-not-typed-in "No date was assumed. The last mismatching file is data/wm-trace/wm-trace-2026-07-09.edn and the first agreeing one is wm-trace-2026-07-14.edn; no file straddles. futon2 9d8f2dee, dated 2026-07-14 and titled 'Repair AIF controls and authoritative substrate wiring', is ONE commit that did BOTH things at once -- it replaced `variance` (sample variance about the mean, /n) with `regularized-error-variance` and flipped default-salience-mode from :summed to :separate. The corpus points at the commit before the commit was looked up."
    :what-that-does-to-the-proved-bound "MachinePrecision.lean proves, under the shipped defaults, that the min-variance branch of this row's own :formal line is never taken (defaultsMinVarianceInert), that the cap is never taken (defaultsCapInert), that Pi <= 21 (defaultsLeTwentyOne), and that the floor is the one reachable bound (floorIsReached). Every one of those is TRUE OF HEAD and this slice re-derived them independently. Over the recorded history they read the other way round: 5175 of 6534 values are above 21.0, 2192 sit at exactly 100.0 -- which is 1/min-variance, the branch proved inert -- the maximum is 105.0, which is 100.0 plus the need term at need-scale 5.0, and the floor 0.1 is reached ZERO times in 6534 (receipt :production-M2)."
    :why-this-is-not-a-refutation-of-the-certificate "The certificate is not false and is not claimed here to be. machinePrecision is the map HEAD runs, the readback re-ran green and byte-identical at this HEAD, and the row's :lean-note already says in terms that the inertness is a property of the DEFAULTS and not of the formula. What is missing is any statement, in the registry row, in the certificate, or in the trace records themselves, that the history the machine will be judged on was produced by a different map. A reader who takes 'Pi <= 21' for a property of the trace is wrong on 79% of it."}
   :the-document-that-grades-r7-describes-the-superseded-map-in-every-particular
   ["docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:181 grades R7 '**Satisfied as of v0.12 (2026-05-18) for the 4 channels with R3a likelihood models**'. The channel count is 8 and has been since futon2 3667dcde (2026-05-30) -- the same commit slice 5 found under-reported at R3 -- and the corpus carries eight on 741 of the 884 records with a :precision-state, six on 17 and four on 126 (receipt :production-M1)."
